WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.867
New pictures

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.334
now of

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.403
Donald Trump inside the car

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:04.604
as he was being driven

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.006
to the courthouse in Miami

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.707
waving to the camera.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:08.675
This was not long before

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.011
he was actually arrested

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:11.845
inside the building

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.113
on federal criminal charges.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.848
Let's get some perspective

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.282
on what the former president

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.384
is going through today

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:19.219
from some veterans of the Trump

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:19.686
White House.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.354
Former White House press secretary

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.689
Stephanie Grisham,

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.090
former deputy White House press

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.625
secretary Sarah Matthews,

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.893
both join me now.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:29.362
Stephanie, let me start with you.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:32.265
Trump in some ways

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:34.834
seems to try to relish moments like this.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.803
He seems to try to spin the narrative.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:39.372
He talks about how they're out to get him

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.206
because they're really out

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.275
to get the American people, etc.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.511
But I have to say, in the in the images

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.413
we saw from the Doral,

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:48.848
he seemed rather dejected.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.985
What do you think, Sara?

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.420
What do you think he's going through?

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.822
I do think that there is a

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.090
sense of normalcy

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.292
sometimes in the chaos and Trump world.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:00.593
It's not like

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.995
they haven't been through this before,

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.596
not just with the first indictment

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.230
in the Alvin

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:04.964
Bragg case,

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.766
but you look at the two impeachment

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.401
proceedings that he went through.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:11.171
So I do think that they are kind of

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.740
used to knowing how to operate

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.241
in these kinds of situations.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.709
They know the drill.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:17.444
But certainly

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:17.744
I think

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.979
this is to a more serious degree

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.648
than what he's faced previously.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:24.951
And Stephanie, what do you think

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.719
Well, I would agree with Sarah.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:27.120
You know,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.222
I think he's absolutely dejected.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.190
I think that was a perfect word

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.291
for you to use.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.625
He doesn't want to be arrested.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.660
I think he even just said that

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.694
on an interview somewhere.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:35.762
He doesn't like that.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.497
He thinks that it's not elegant.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:38.998
He thinks that it takes away

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.266
some of his power deep down.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.068
So he definitely doesn't like it.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.269
But being Trump,

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.070
he's going to double,

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.605
triple down as he's been doing

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.073
and he's going to fundraise off of it.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.108
He's going to play the victim,

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.476
as you just said.

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:51.511
And I did think it was really interesting

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.479
that earlier

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:53.012
it was said that

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.380
he's keeping people closer

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.015
I think he's got to be feeling

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.318
pretty desperate right now.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.086
He doesn't have a lot of staff.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.454
People are scared.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.389
People are getting in real trouble.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.657
And I think that's weighing heavily

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.092
on his mind as well.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.660
Sarah, how did you see him

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.062
treat classified documents?

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.530
Does any of this

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.831
come as a surprise to you?

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:13.399
This wasn't

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.033
something that

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.069
I was necessarily privy to in my role

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.737
being in the press office.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:18.872
But I do think that

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.073
if we know anything about Trump,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.808
he wasn't your typical president

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:22.542
and he didn't

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.144
always follow procedures

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:26.446
and the norms of the institution.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:27.747
So I wouldn't

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.249
be surprised if that were the case.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.251
As this indictment clearly lays out.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.353
Stephanie, Trump is

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:36.122
is not the only defendant today.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.357
His aide,

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:38.691
while Nada, is also

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.660
part of the federal indictment.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.296
It is rare, but we have seen

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:44.964
some people

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:45.865
who were part of Trump

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.767
world flip on Trump before.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.503
Michael Cohen comes to mind right now.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.939
But but as of this moment, not

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:55.008
he seems to be staying loyal to Trump.

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.009
Do you know anything about

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:56.876
their relationship?

00:02:58.611 --> 00:02:59.512
Well, they were always

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.847
close in the White House.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:01.915
Of course,

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:04.284
he was his usher and personal aide.

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:06.886
So he would be around him all the time.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.720
More specifically,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.122
when we traveled and do,

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.456
you know, go into the hotel rooms

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.292
and you get a lot of one on one time

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.960
with with the most powerful man

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:14.894
in the world

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.197
in a way that nobody else really does.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:19.132
So I believe that they're very close.

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:20.133
But I think what people need

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:20.900
to remember is

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:21.668
and this was alluded

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.102
to in the previous interview

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.070
or the previous reporter

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.505
said he's got to be

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:28.141
what has got to be feeling trapped

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.342
even a little bit right now.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.244
It is very expensive

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:33.379
to have to hire attorneys to fight.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.248
Of course, the justice system,

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.016
but also to fight Donald Trump.

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.618
He's famous for people

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.220
keeping people up in litigation.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.888
I mean, I have been

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.523
subject to it and it's terrifying.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:44.390
And if you don't have

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.992
the finances to do it,

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.760
you're going to take any free lawyer

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.294
you can get.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.028
And then another thing

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.196
I'll say is to leave

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.798
that circle has got to be scary

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:53.066
right now, too,

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.234
because it's all hands on deck

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.635
and the wagons are circling.

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:56.669
Sara, do you think

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:59.372
Nada is someone

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:02.041
Trump can trust

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.043
who is, you know, Enthrall,

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.645
who believes all the crazy election

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:07.847
lies, etc., etc..

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:10.250
Or is it possible that that he might flip

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.819
John Dean from Watergate?

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.154
Fame was on the show yesterday

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.889
and said that his message to not

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.758
it would be get your own lawyer

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:19.892
and start cooperating

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.262
so that you don't have to go down

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.663
with the ship.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.565
I don't know, Walt, not personally.

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:27.867
So I can't speak to where his mind is

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:28.835
and how supportive

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:29.669
he is of everything

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:30.203
Trump says

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.205
or does with the election lies

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.273
and things like that.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.907
But I do agree with that advice.

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:36.009
I think if we know anything

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.143
about Donald Trump,

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:39.145
loyalty is a one way street with him.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.580
He demands it from everyone

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.948
but gives it to no one.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.583
And so I hope that Walt

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:44.984
not is getting sound

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.486
advice from his loved ones

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.187
around him to hire a lawyer

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:49.656
that is looking in

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:50.890
for his best interests

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.659
rather than Trump's best interests.

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:54.027
And that's typically what happens

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.628
when you have a Trump paid lawyer.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.230
For example, you look at Cassidy

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:57.997
Hutchinson,

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.132
one of the key witnesses

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.301
in the January six committee.

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:03.303
She had a Trump lawyer at first,

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.671
and they were encouraging her

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:07.006
to do things to help out Trump,

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:09.242
not to help out her.

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:09.876
One of the things

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:10.276
I'm wondering

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:10.877
for both of you

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:11.477
and I'll start with you,

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:14.280
Stephanie, has to do with your reaction

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.181
to the indictment,

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.450
the description of how Trump behaved,

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.052
bringing these boxes,

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.119
showing off,

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.120
according to the indictment,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.789
classified information

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.924
to just people in the room with him

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:27.460
seemingly to push back on accusations

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:27.994
against him

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.462
or to impress them

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:31.130
telling aides to lie,

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.699
according to the indictment,

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:34.801
about turning over the documents

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.369
to the FBI, etc..

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:37.770
Was there anything in there

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.839
that surprised you and and why?

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.507
That's the big question. Why?

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.642
Why did Donald Trump

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.677
not just give these documents back?

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.079
He would have avoided all of this.

00:05:46.079 --> 00:05:46.546
Stephanie?

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:48.481
Well, my

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:50.383
short answer is no, not any of it

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:51.584
surprised me at all.

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:52.552
Rang true.

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.986
Even, you know, the

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:54.320
why don't

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.688
we just take those documents out?

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:56.856
It wouldn't be a problem, right?

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:58.591
That's so him

00:05:58.591 --> 00:05:58.991
And then,

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:01.260
you know, I saw him all the time.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.562
The public saw him all the time.

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:03.062
Think about

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.397
when we were looking at,

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:06.399
you know, information about China

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.034
at Mar a Lago.

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:09.736
And South Korea in North Korea.

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:11.371
I mean, he talks about it all the time.

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:12.538
Why didn't he give them back?

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.474
It's because he thinks

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:15.308
those are his

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:16.209
he's like a child

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:18.211
holding on to his little toy train.

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:20.313
And nobody's going to take it from him.

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.382
My reaction is I'm very upset,

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:23.383
especially when I saw

00:06:23.383 --> 00:06:24.250
those pictures, Jake.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:24.951
You know,

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:26.886
I practically lived at Mar a Lago.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:28.354
And so some of those

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.289
those places that I saw, I was

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:31.891
I mean, I was even surprised for Trump

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:32.492
that they could have been

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:34.894
so, so careless with those documents.

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:37.163
We heard some just.

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:38.264
I'll go to Sara in a second.

00:06:38.264 --> 00:06:39.465
But we heard Congressman

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.100
Byron Donalds today

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.368
and also Speaker McCarthy

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:43.569
saying, Stephanie,

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:43.736
know,

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:45.104
the bathroom door is lock

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:45.938
and you guys are making

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.907
too big a deal out of this

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:48.474
we don't you know

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:50.576
there are 33 bathrooms in at Mar a Lago.

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.612
Stephanie, as somebody who spent

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:53.212
a lot of time in Mar

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:54.480
a Lago, is that is that right

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:58.484
Well, there are a lot of bathrooms.

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.119
You're in guest rooms.

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:00.753
That bathroom

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:02.255
particularly was also a room

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:04.457
that guest would play bridge

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:05.558
and poker in.

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:06.759
And so I guarantee

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:07.760
when there were guests

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.562
in that room, that door wasn't locked.

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:10.496
And most specifically,

00:07:10.496 --> 00:07:12.031
the stage in the ballroom,

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:13.533
that's the one that really got me

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:14.767
a ballroom is right next

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.702
to a pool where all of the guests are.

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:17.403
And it's got,

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.138
I think, four doors

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:21.107
that none were usually locked.

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:23.176
And it was sitting on a stage

00:07:23.176 --> 00:07:24.277
right out in the open.

00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:25.411
So you know,

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:26.045
I understand

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:26.679
that they're trying

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:27.780
to defend Donald Trump,

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.415
but there's absolutely no defense

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:30.750
for the way this was stored.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.117
And Sara

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:32.852
Matthews, your reaction to the indictment

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:35.354
and your answer to my question, why

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:37.657
Why would he do this?

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:38.825
I think that this indictment

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:40.626
kind of perfectly encapsulates

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:41.828
Donald Trump in a way

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:43.529
that he would think

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:44.997
that these documents were his

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.866
he called them my boxes.

00:07:46.866 --> 00:07:47.567
He didn't think that

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.001
he needed to give them back.

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:49.469
And that's

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:50.403
what's so disturbing

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:51.871
about this indictment is

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:53.473
he could have avoided this.

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:55.508
It's 100% self inflicted.

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:57.343
If he had just returned the documents

00:07:57.343 --> 00:07:58.444
when asked,

00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:00.046
then he wouldn't be finding himself

00:08:00.046 --> 00:08:01.380
in this situation.

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.448
Sara Matthews and Stephanie

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:03.516
Grisham, as always,

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:04.817
thank you so much for your perspective

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:05.952
and your insight. Appreciate it.

